 by one person through self-study (poor development team)</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Known problems and solutions:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If operating with the mouse, please unplug the gamepad or Bluetooth transmitter.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the game crashes, increase the system's virtual memory.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solution for not finding SAVE:</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Please select &quot;Browse Local Files&quot; on STEAM.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Open the &quot;BlurredWeirdNight_DatadataSavedGame&quot; folder.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Move all the save files to another folder for backup.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Keep only the last numbered save file. (Generally, the save file is 460K in size. If there is a 0K save file, delete it directly.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For example, if the last save file is &quot;Save68.sav&quot;, rename it to &quot;Save0.sav&quot;.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(The &quot;.sav&quot; is the file extension. If it's not displayed on some systems, just rename it to &quot;Save0&quot;.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then you can successfully load the game when you enter the game again.</p>", "short_description": "I thought it was a comedy, but it turned out to be a tragedy. If there's a chance to go back in time and change something that would cause lifelong regret, would you fight with all you have? (Including story mode and zombie mode)", "supported_languages": "English, French, German, Spanish - Spain, Russian, Japanese, Simplified Chinese<strong>*</strong>, Traditional Chinese<strong>*</strong>, Portuguese - Portugal<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1448000/2702385f4053630abb8efafad09273a4a3d9114d/header.jpg?t=1787829922", "capsule_image": "https://shar